    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **38 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp27Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` field so it returns `'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`.\n\nSince `OwnerDto` is generated from the OpenAPI spec at build time (following the existing pattern used by `membershipLevel`, `locality`, etc.), the change was two parts:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `contactPreference` property to the `Owner` schema (a string enum of `EMAIL`/`PHONE`, `readOnly`), which the code generator turns into `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes the value: `EMAIL` when `owner.getEmail()` is non-null and non-empty, otherwise `PHONE`. This mirrors the exact email-presence check already used for `membershipLevel`, so it stays consistent with the app's normalization (email is null when absent).\n\nThe response DTO is the same one returned by both `POST /api/owners` and `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so the field is populated on read as the tests expect.",
